OK, dev team people -- if you're lurking out there, please listen up!
As a nethack addict who is destroying her wrists, eyes, and neck  
(not to mention brain) playing nethack 3.1, I have a few suggestions to
make.

1)  I appreciate having my strength, constitution, and dexterity go up
from time to time.  But the fluctuations of wisdom are damn annoying.  If
wisdom mattered in this game it might be more important to increase it.
If you're going to subject us constantly to "You feel foolish!  You must
not have been paying attention" why not make wisdom more important.  Give
us some kind of savings throw against nymph charm.  A wisdom of 18 ought
to give the character immunity or at least the chance to run away before
she steals anything.

2)  On this same subject, how about this:  eating a mind flayer corpse
increases your intelligence by one point (apart from intelligence points
it may have sucked out of your brain).  

3) To carry the idea further:  gain charisma either by going up levels
(power is attractive) or by eating the corpses of charismatic creatures
like nymphs.

4)  Instant-death poison darts are really annoying.  I don't see the 
point of this trap.  My valkyrie is happily wandering through the mines
when *bam* a poison dart hits her and she's dead.  This is a real
turn-off!!!

5)  Change the game interface so that a message stays up on the board
until another one comes along.  My left shoulder is hurting from all the 
Ctrl-P-ing I have to do.  

6)  When frozen or put to sleep, it's really depressing having to hit
the space bar repeatedly watching critters slowly erode hit points away,
wondering if your level 13 Priest is going to wake up in time.  I wish
there was a better way to display what's going on in this situation --
maybe instead of going through line after line of "the gnome hits you -- more"
the game could carry out the combat invisibly and finally come back with
either "You can move again" or "You were killed in your sleep . . ."
And while we're at it, the period of enforced sleep should be shortened.  
Most people wake up pretty soon when they're being hacked at.  Wands of
sleep are more like wands of unconsciousness.

7)  Whatever you do, don't make the game any harder!!  I've gotten through
the quest once.  A total of 5 players have ascended in Nethack 3.1 on the
three public machines here at the University of Chicago.  PLEASE PLEASE
PLEASE DON'T MAKE IT EVEN TOUGHER! 

Have at it, folks.
